cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use lpbench, please cite it as below."
title: lpbench
abstract: >-
  An honest CPU benchmark of open-source LP solvers (HiGHS, OR-Tools GLOP and
  PDLP, SCIP/SoPlex) on Netlib and MIPLIB 2017 LP relaxations: every reported
  optimum independently verified, performance variability measured across seeds
  and permutations, and bootstrap intervals on shifted geometric means and
  performance profiles.
type: software
authors:
  - name: lpbench contributors
repository-code: "https://github.com/h-a-forster/lpbench"
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
keywords:
  - linear programming
  - benchmarking
  - performance profiles
  - bootstrap
  - performance variability
